    howTo: [{"name":"Enter amount","text":"Type amount like 100 or 1000, for example 100 USD for European trip budgeting and expense planning purposes."},{"name":"Pick pair","text":"Choose from currency USD and to currency EUR, or INR to USD, using searchable dropdown menus for 150 options."},{"name":"View","text":"Read converted total like 92 EUR instantly with rate stamp, then compare reverse pair to understand spread clearly."},{"name":"Try an example","text":"Convert 100 USD to EUR and 1000 INR to USD, then swap pair to compare reverse rates effectively."}],
    guide: [{ heading: "What rate swaps show", body: "Converter translates 150 global currencies using live market quotes with timestamp plus resilient cached fallback for offline travel planning. Example 1: enter 100 USD to EUR at sample 0.92, receive about 92 EUR for hotel budgeting across Paris itineraries. Example 2: enter 1000 INR to USD at 0.012, receive about 12 USD for freelance payout estimation and remittance planning. Importers price 20 goods, students budget semesters, tourists compare pocket money across borders daily. Live fetch contacts rate API only; amounts compute locally, never upload, history clears on closure. Interface lists symbols, flags, and decimal precision, supports swapping pairs instantly. Backpackers track spending, finance clubs model scenarios, families plan relocations responsibly with educational estimates. Backpackers compare hostels, expats remit salaries, and shoppers evaluate import duties prudently. See /terms; informational only, not financial advice." }, { heading: "How live plus cache pair", body: "Live mode requests fresh quotes via network in one fetch, displaying provider and timestamp for transparency and audit. Reference pair table: 100 USD equals 92 EUR sample | 1000 INR equals 12 USD sample | 50 GBP equals 60 EUR sample | 200 EUR equals 216 USD sample | 5000 JPY equals 33 USD sample. Cached mode substitutes last stored rates when offline, flagging age prominently to prevent stale decisions. Amounts never leave browser; only rate request hits network. Flip pairs to compare spreads, monitor intraday drift, and screenshot stamps for records. Edge case: cached rates age quickly during volatility; revalidate before large transfers, verify bank fees and spreads separately. See /terms; quotes educational, not trading advice. Analysts track trends, accountants reconcile statements, travelers screenshot stamps, and students learn forex basics responsibly." }, { heading: "Currency worked example: 100 USD is 92 EUR", body: "Example 1: type 100 USD to EUR to see about 92 EUR at 0.92 sample, swap to EUR-USD to confirm reverse near 108.70. Example 2: type 1000 INR to USD for about 12 USD at 0.012 sample supporting payout planning. Edge case: exotic pairs update less frequently and round to fewer decimals; confirm with provider before invoicing. Limitation: informational estimates only, excluding fees, spreads, settlement delays, or execution guarantees for 150 pairs. For unit math visit converter at /unit-converter; for travel time planning explore converter at /timezone-converter, both offline companions. Always verify live bank rates before committing funds. Compare total costs including wire fees, card markups, and weekend surcharges carefully every time. See /terms; this content is educational and not financial advice." }]
